From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eTran experiment <etran-experiment@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:08:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net/mlx5e: use async ICOSQ for affinity change IRQ

Backport the locked async ICOSQ wakeup from Linux 6.6.y (upstream c326f9c68921), limited to the existing affinity-change branch. Gate the kick while the asynchronous SQ is disabled.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_txrx.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_txrx.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_txrx.c
index d25b2fb..dce5e26 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_txrx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_txrx.c
@@ -247,8 +247,9 @@ int mlx5e_napi_poll(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget)
 		mlx5e_cq_arm(&xskrq->cq);
 	}
 
-	if (unlikely(aff_change && busy_xsk)) {
-		mlx5e_trigger_irq(&c->icosq);
+	if (unlikely(aff_change && busy_xsk) &&
+	    test_bit(MLX5E_SQ_STATE_ENABLED, &c->async_icosq.state)) {
+		mlx5e_trigger_napi_icosq(c);
 		ch_stats->force_irq++;
 	}
 
